    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — `@m0saic/alpine/stat-card/v1`** (gate 10; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Props = showcase defaults (Commits 1,243 +12.4%). Single version — no dep riders.\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | not internal, not deprecated, primitive:true | confirm |\n| Gate | — | **base** |\n| Preview assets | re-mint after approval | review |\n| Cover / Tutorial | cover BUILT this gate (count-up starts at 0) | eyeball cover; tutorial needed? |\n\n**Pre-audit found + fixed 3:**\n1. **Portrait proportion breakdown**: bands are height-fractions, so tall cards minted a ~195px icon chip towering over its width-capped label, and a 73px delta triangle beside 17px text. Chip now caps at 0.18·min-dim (square, band-centered); arrow sized in two passes to ≤1.25× the delta font. Landscape defaults byte-identical (caps sit above the default values).\n2. **Wide-script caps**: capFont counted flat chars — Cyrillic labels would clip (the gate-9 lesson). Now textEmUnits-based + floor-bound ellipsis on all four texts.\n3. Unused node:path import dropped; cover added (static default card + welcome band).\n\n**PRIMITIVE-SENSE — the real question this gate: the pack now has TWO KPI cards.** `kpi-card/v2` (shipped base ☑, gate 6: label/value/delta PILL + sparkline, alpineCard chrome) vs `stat-card/v1` (icon chip + label / value / triangle delta + sublabel, placeRect-EXACT geometry, geometry-contract, built to NEST in hero dashboard grids — the FFmpeg pulse tiles). My recommendation: KEEP BOTH as base — kpi-card is the standalone showcase card, stat-card is the nestable dashboard tile; the exact-geometry construction + transparent-surface + showHeader-style composability serve a different role. Alternative if you want ONE: stat-card could ride base·int (internal, hero-pack building block). Your call.\n\nALSO SURFACED (infra, not this gate): a template that THROWS (e.g. unknown icon name) renders a BLACK mp4 at exit 1 via the CLI — reported, but the error card pixels are lost when the error doc rides as a resolver child. Filed as a candidate note.\n\nBattery: 84/84 CLI feasible ×2 (pre+post fix; success-grep hardened — \"Render completed with errors\" no longer counts as a pass), probe 14/14 green (geometry-contract stamps), 23/23 unit.",
